    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0602" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg518"/>

                <head>No. 266.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Woodbury.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 31,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to acknowledge your letter of
                    yesterday accompanied by the affidavit of Alexander McDonald and eleven others,
                    members of the crew of the schooner Thomas F. Bayard, of Gloucester, stating the
                    refusal of the local officials at Bonne Bay, Newfoundland, to permit fishing or
                    the purchase of bait on that coast.</p>
                <p>The subject to which this paper relates received due attention yesterday, as you
                    were advised.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
